<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 172 0 R
/E (The Entity-Relationship diagram illustrates the core database structure of our Restaurant Management System. Key entities include Customers, Employees, Menu_Items, Orders, Order_Details, Reservations, Inventory, and Payments. Critical relationships connect Orders to both Customers and Menu_Items, while Order_Details links individual items to their parent orders. Reservations reference both Customers and table availability, and Payments are tied to completed Orders. This relational structure ensures data integrity and enables efficient querying across all restaurant operations.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
